    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_574b44a32e96858e3d158e45aa8aa5cd4a38bbf06cbdb5105b2e5b2c0e441a7b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Compact support turns each Weil-form test into a finite-prime variational problem. If its lowest eigenvalue is simple and isolated with an even eigenfunction, the ground-state transform has only line-constrained zeros; the prolate construction separately supplies explicit candidates whose transforms converge to Xi, so proving that those candidates approximate the true Weil ground states would connect finite-prime real-zero surrogates to Xi.",
