    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_dbf81669c6123284b20de5652ddc87d9fa66242516b7569703656f7913a8b3df",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Random-matrix comparisons and operator models interrogate different invariants of the zeta zeros: height-dependent unfolding exposes local correlations (with symmetry selected at the level of L-function families), whereas the prolate/Dirac construction targets ultraviolet spectral counting and the RH-conditional heat expansion records high-energy invariants. Agreement in one normalized statistic or asymptotic regime therefore does not identify a full fixed zeta-spectrum operator.",
